  "term": "ethchlorvynol",
  "definition": "Ethchlorvynol is a sedative-hypnotic substance in the tertiary carbinol class. It appears to reduce central nervous system activity by acting at the benzodiazepine–GABA-A chloride channel receptor complex, which increases chloride entry into neurons and lowers their excitability.",
